 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T07:01+08:00",
 "answer": "**Probably not by much.** For Saturday, October 17, Singapore’s NEA forecasts a 24-hour PSI of **150–230**—still **unhealthy to very unhealthy**, broadly similar to tonight’s 159–222. Showers and shifting winds may reduce some smoke from Kalimantan, but haze from Sumatra could still drift in. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nIf you’re planning to be outdoors, check the latest 1-hour PM2.5 readings tomorrow; NEA advises avoiding prolonged or strenuous outdoor activity. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
